+  Two rules make such counters work:
+  - When a duration is made of repeated shorter periods (a prescaler or
+    divider tick, a bit time, a beat), count those periods, not raw clock
+    cycles, and check the length of one period in its own property. A
+    counter of raw clocks over hundreds of cycles is no easier to check than
+    an unrolled window.
+  - Also assert, in every cycle, how your counter corresponds to the
+    design's own progress state (its own counter or phase), so that every
+    timing property only needs to look one cycle ahead.
 - **Timing.** `a |-> b` checks `b` in the same cycle as `a`; `a |=> b` checks
   it in the next cycle; a register assigned with `<=` shows its new value one
   cycle after the condition. Check each alignment against the RTL by hand.
